from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,json
base=Path('terms/OT1998/sources/chunk8-comparator');out=Path('terms/OT1998/sources/chunk8-neutral-control')
def clean(n):return '\n'.join('\n'.join(x.strip().splitlines()[3:]) for x in (base/(n+'-official.txt')).read_text(encoding='utf-8').split('\f'))
def cut(t,a,b):return t[t.index(a):t.index(b,t.index(a))]
t=clean('white');white=cut(t,'On three occasions in July and August 1993','We granted certiorari,')
# This span includes the reporter's source quotations of sections 932.703(1)(a) and (2)(a), including qualifications.
(out/'WHITE_OBJECTIVE_EXTRACT.txt').write_text(white,encoding='utf-8')
t=clean('ruhrgas');ruhr=cut(t[t.index('\nI\nThe underlying controversy stems from a venture')+3:],'The underlying controversy stems from a venture','We granted certiorari, 525 U. S. 1039')
(out/'RUHRGAS_OBJECTIVE_EXTRACT.txt').write_text(ruhr,encoding='utf-8')
p=out/'SOURCE_STATUS.md';p.write_text(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')+'\n- **White supplemental extract (526 U.S. 561–563):** The accepted factual recitation supplies probable cause that the vehicle had been used for cocaine delivery. It does not supply present probable cause that cocaine remained inside. The vehicle seizure and later inventory search are distinct. The quoted statute permits seizure and directs forfeiture; these verbs are not interchangeable. The quoted section 932.703(2)(a) ties seizure to notice of the right to a postseizure adversarial probable-cause hearing. The source quote contains its own ellipsis, which is retained and not represented as a complete copy of the entire section. The proceeding is the possession prosecution and suppression ruling, not a final adjudication of forfeiture.\n- **Ruhrgas supplemental extract (526 U.S. 578–582):** Three asserted removal grounds remain distinct: diversity with alleged fraudulent joinder of Norge, federal-common-law international-relations questions, and section 205 international-arbitration removal. The district court dismissed for lack of personal jurisdiction after jurisdictional discovery. Its no-tortious-Texas-conduct and insufficient systematic/continuous-contacts conclusions are lower-court findings, not facts newly decided here. The original panel rejected all removal grounds, but its judgment was vacated on en banc rehearing. The en banc court required subject-matter jurisdiction first and remanded to the district court, expressly reserving the panel’s jurisdictional conclusions.\n',encoding='utf-8')
r=json.loads((out/'COPY_RECEIPT.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'));r['artifacts']={p.name:hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() for p in out.iterdir() if p.is_file() and p.name!='COPY_RECEIPT.json'};(out/'COPY_RECEIPT.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
